["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Most white tails are seen in the first and last hour of light. Be in place before those hours, not during them.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock with midnight at the top. Daylight is pale, night is dark. Orange bands show movement peaks around dawn, about 05:30 to 08:30, and dusk, about 16:00 to 19:30. In the middle of the day the deer is bedded. At night it feeds in fields.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A fall day, valley white tail</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#3b4a5c\"/><path d=\"M296.6 181.9 A 100 100 0 0 1 100.0 156.0 L200.0 156.0 A 0 0 0 0 0 200.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#f6e7b8\"/><path d=\"M299.1 142.9 A 100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L249.2 193.7 A 62 62 0 0 0 261.5 147.9 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M113.4 206.0 A 100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L142.7 132.3 A 62 62 0 0 0 146.3 187.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M241.0 197.0 A 58 58 0 0 1 154.0 191.3 L179.4 171.8 A 26 26 0 0 0 218.4 174.4 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M149.8 127.0 A 58 58 0 0 1 253.6 133.8 L224.0 146.1 A 26 26 0 0 0 177.5 143.0 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">00:00</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">06:00</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12:00</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18:00</text><text x=\"275.13776940828177\" y=\"165.74079978861175\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dawn</text><text x=\"118.46016078906504\" y=\"174.78039091448292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusk</text><text x=\"197.80188983779635\" y=\"197.9424404596921\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bedded</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: moving. Peaks near first and last light.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Peaks near dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Midday: bedded and chewing cud <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Bed to feed to water: the daily loop.</li><li>How the day shifts with season.</li><li>Weather: wind, rain, snow, cold fronts, barometric pressure, with the evidence level for each.</li><li>The moon. Hunting pressure.</li><li>A hunter's day plan.</li><li>Mule deer days in open country: <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-06\">Mule deer Masterclass 6</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, bird's eye view. A deer starts bedded in timber at the top. At dusk it walks down the trail to the open feeding field and feeds through the night. At dawn it walks back up the same trail to bed. Final label: hunt the line between bed and feed, near the feed at dusk, near the bed at dawn.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"80,95 92,57 104,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"350,95 362,57 374,95\"/><polygon points=\"250,90 262,52 274,90\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed: open field</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"44\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <text x=\"198\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed: timber</text>\n  <path id=\"sg-bed-feed-down\" d=\"M200 95 C 240 130, 160 170, 210 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <path id=\"sg-bed-feed-loop\" d=\"M200 95 C 240 130, 160 170, 210 250 C 160 170, 240 130, 200 95\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"38\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Day: bedded, chewing cud\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"1.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f2a56b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Dusk: down to feed\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#cfd8e6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Night: feeding in the open\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Dawn: back up to bed\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <ellipse rx=\"13\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-5\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <animateMotion dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\" keyPoints=\"0;0;0.5;0.5;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1875;0.5;0.6875;1\"><mpath href=\"#sg-bed-feed-loop\"/></animateMotion>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"215\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You at dusk</text>\n    <circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"130\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"259\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You at dawn</text>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"258\" width=\"320\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt the line between</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Bed in cover, feed in the field, back at dawn. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Feed in fields late afternoon into the night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Back to willow and cottonwood beds by first light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily loop</summary><ul><li>Evening: leave bedding cover, stage at the edge, enter the field near dark <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Night: feed in hay and alfalfa, browse along edges <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dawn: drift back to bedding cover at or before first light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Midday: bedded, chewing cud, getting up to stretch and nibble now and then <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Water: deer drink about 3 lb of water per lb of dry food, but only half a pound per lb of green food (80%, Montana State University Extension). In a valley bottom water is never far (Tip).</li><li>Penn State October data: about 120 to 140 m an hour at dawn and dusk, under 50 m an hour midday, about 60 m an hour at night (75%, via <a href=\"#/s/fronts-and-movement\">Weather fronts</a>).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th>Pattern</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer</td><td>Dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Fall</td><td>Dawn, dusk, night fields <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Rut</td><td>Any hour, midday too <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Winter</td><td>Active most of the day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Winter deer feed in the warm midday sun (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why the pattern shifts</summary><ul><li>BC account: \"In summer, they are more active at dawn and dusk, but in winter they are active most of the day\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Starkey, Oregon (deer and elk): activity peaks about 04:00 to 09:00 and 17:00 to 21:00 (85%, Stewart and others 2002).</li><li>Rut bucks search for does at all hours <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Winter: short days and cold push feeding into the warmest hours (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Rating chart of how strongly studies link each factor to deer movement, out of 5. Time of day 5, strong. Season and rut 5, strong. Hunting pressure 4, strong. Temperature 3, some. Wind 2, mixed. Barometric pressure 2, mixed. Moon 1, weak.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What moves deer? Strength of evidence</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Time of day</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"46\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"46\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"46\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"46\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"46\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">strong</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Season, rut</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"80\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"80\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"80\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"80\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"80\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">strong</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunting pressure</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">strong</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Temperature</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">some</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"182\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"182\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"182\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"182\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"182\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">mixed</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Barometer</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"216\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"216\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"216\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"216\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"216\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"231\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">mixed</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moon</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"250\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"198\" y=\"250\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"250\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"250\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"250\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">weak</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">GPS collar studies, 2026 reading. See More.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Time of day and season beat any weather effect <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Weather effects are real but small and mixed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the studies</summary><ul><li>Auburn University thesis (South Carolina GPS, Global Positioning System, collars): weather, temperature, wind, pressure and moon mattered only in some seasons and hours, and less than the daily rhythm (75%, search preview).</li><li>Mississippi Department of Wildlife, Fisheries and Parks: across many deer and a whole season, weather effects are weaker than hunters think. Very high barometric pressure went with more winter buck movement <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Penn State: does through 30 winter storms showed no change before storms and moved less during them (80%, via <a href=\"#/s/fronts-and-movement\">Weather fronts</a>).</li><li>Oklahoma collar study: temperature explained most of the change in movement <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Rating in the chart is my reading of these studies, not a published score (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Your scent drifts like campfire smoke, away from a feeding deer. Then the light wind shifts and the scent plume swings toward the deer. The deer's head comes up and it bounds away. Light, shifting wind is the danger.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Scent drifts like smoke</text>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 120 220;0 120 220;-111 120 220;-111 120 220\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;0.65;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M120 220 L230 190 L230 260 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".55\">\n      <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"222\" r=\"4\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"130;225\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></circle>\n      <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"210\" r=\"4\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"130;225\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\".7s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"218;198\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\".7s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></circle>\n      <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"232\" r=\"4\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"130;225\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\"1.3s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"222;250\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\"1.3s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></circle>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n  <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"220\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 0;160 -40\" keyTimes=\"0;0.8;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(70 90)\"><ellipse rx=\"20\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"6;6;-12;-12\" keyTimes=\"0;0.68;0.72;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.2s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <text x=\"388\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\">Wind shifts...</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"230\" width=\"190\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"295\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Busted. Light, shifting</text>\n    <text x=\"295\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind is the danger</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A wind shift moves your scent cone. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Strong wind: deer bed tighter, move less <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Light rain: deer often still move (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wind, rain, snow</summary><ul><li>One South Texas radio collar study: movement dropped sharply at about 24 to 31 km/h (15 to 19 mph) wind, then rebounded above about 32 km/h (60%, secondary report).</li><li>An Oklahoma collar study found little change in distance moved with wind speed (60%, secondary report).</li><li>So wind effects are mixed. Wind matters most because it carries your scent and covers your sound (Tip).</li><li>Rain: Penn State preliminary notes: bucks moved less in rain than does <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>First snow: fresh tracks show exactly where deer are moving. Great scouting (Tip, see <a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking\">Snow tracking</a>).</li><li>Deep snow over about 40 cm pushes white tails onto winter range and packed trails <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 250\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart. Penn State collared does showed no real change in movement before 30 winter storms and moved less during them. Glassing the calm after is a tip, not a finding.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"250\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Collared deer around a storm</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"64\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Day before the storm</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"70\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"243.2\" y=\"85\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">no real change</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"116\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">During the storm</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"122\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"131.6\" y=\"137\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">moved less</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"168\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Calm after the storm</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"174\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"243.2\" y=\"189\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">glass it (Tip)</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"226\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Penn State, 30 storms, collared does (80%). After</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"242\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">the storm: Tip only.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>\"Feed before the front\" is not proven <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A hard cold snap after a warm spell: watch for daylight feeding (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: front detail</summary><ul><li>Penn State storm study: no change before winter storms <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Mississippi: very high pressure correlated with more winter buck movement <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hunter consensus: the day after a cold front clears, with rising pressure and cold calm air, is a great morning to sit (Tip, widely repeated, weak evidence).</li><li>Hot October days: deer bed in shade and move at the edges of legal light (Tip).</li><li>Log temperature, pressure and wind in the Journal each sit. Your own valley data beats any article (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Mississippi State data on 48 collared bucks. The moon changed movement by about 4 metres an hour, a sliver of a bar, inside the GPS error. The rut nearly doubled buck travel, a long bar. Rut beats moon.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Buck travel: moon versus rut</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Normal</text>\n  <rect x=\"110\" y=\"62\" width=\"130\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Moon</text>\n  <rect x=\"110\" y=\"116\" width=\"130\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"116\" width=\"4\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  <text x=\"252\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">about 4 m an hour</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Rut</text>\n  <rect x=\"110\" y=\"170\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"235\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">nearly double (75%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"12\" y=\"226\" width=\"376\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moon effect is inside the GPS error</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffd34d\" text-anchor=\"middle\">48 bucks, Mississippi State (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>collar studies: dawn and dusk win in every moon phase <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Moon effects, if any, are small <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: moon studies</summary><ul><li>Texas King Ranch: 43 collared bucks showed no moon phase pattern (65%, via Outdoor Life).</li><li>North Carolina State: over 22,000 collar locations, deer moved most at dawn and dusk regardless of phase, with only small midday upticks near the full moon <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Auburn and SEAFWA (Southeastern Association of Fish and Wildlife Agencies) 2016: 38 collared bucks. Small solunar effects that changed with the moon phase; the authors warn solunar charts \"may be misleading\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Penn State: no moon phase link in collared does <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>The moon does not set the rut. Day length does <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>My lean (Tip): ignore the moon. Hunt the wind and the time of year.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Before the opener, deer feed in an open field near the road. On opening day trucks park along the road. The deer move away from the road into thick timber. One hunter walks past the last truck, deep into the thick cover where the deer went.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <path d=\"M240 0 L400 0 L400 300 L270 300 C 250 220, 300 120, 240 0 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".75\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thick timber</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">road</text>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 180;80 180;300 120;300 120\" keyTimes=\"0;0.35;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"130 200;130 200;330 170;330 170\" keyTimes=\"0;0.38;0.72;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"170 160;170 160;350 90;350 90\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Before opening day</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Opener: trucks arrive</text></g>\n  <path id=\"hf-pressure-shift-path\" d=\"M260 261 C 262 230, 262 200, 280 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n  <circle r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateMotion begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\"2.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#hf-pressure-shift-path\"/></animateMotion></circle>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"8.5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"12\" y=\"60\" width=\"210\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk past the last truck</text>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt the thick stuff (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Pressure pushes deer into the thick stuff. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Pressure turns white tails nocturnal and into thick cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Midweek beats the weekend (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure detail</summary><ul><li>Penn State collar study: deer reacted the day before opening and hid inside their home range <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Pressured white tails move more at night and use thicker cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Opening day and weekends push deer from roads and field edges (Tip).</li><li>Hunters moving midday can push deer past a partner on a stand (Tip, see chapter 9).</li><li>Walk 500 m past the road, park quietly, close the truck door with your hip (Tip, matches <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a>).</li><li>More: <a href=\"#/s/pressure-push\">Hunting pressure</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five step timeline of a hunter&#x27;s day, labelled as a tip. 1 before light: walk in quietly and sit. 2 first two hours: stand on the trail. 3 midday: scout or still hunt slowly. 4 two hours before dark: stand near food. 5 after dark: leave without bumping deer. A side box says on rut days stay out all day because bucks also move midday.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A white tail hunter&#x27;s day (Tip)</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"60\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before light</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Walk in quiet, sit</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"34\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"110\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">First 2 h</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stand on the trail</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"34\" y2=\"148\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"160\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midday</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Scout, still hunt slow</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"34\" y2=\"198\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"210\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 h before dark</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stand near food</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"34\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"260\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">After dark</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Leave without bumping</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rut days:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stay out</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">all day, bucks</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">move midday</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">too</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: best odds. Plan the wind for each sit.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>In your seat 30 minutes before legal light (Tip).</li><li>Last 2 hours of light: your best sit (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full day</summary><ol><li>Check the wind and pick the stand that fits it (Tip).</li><li>Walk in on a route that does not cross the deer's path from field to bed (Tip).</li><li>Sit through the first 2 hours of light (Tip).</li><li>Midday: scout, still hunt slowly in thick bottoms, or rest (Tip).</li><li>Back in your evening stand at least 2 hours before dark (Tip).</li><li>Leave after dark without walking through the field the deer are feeding in (Tip).</li></ol><ul><li>Legal hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, synopsis page 11 item 38, via the <a href=\"#/s/white-tailed-deer\">quick lesson</a>).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock with midnight at the top. Daylight is pale, night is dark. Orange bands show movement peaks around dawn, about 05:30 to 08:30, and dusk, about 16:00 to 19:30. In the middle of the day the deer is bedded. At night it feeds in fields.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A fall day, valley white tail</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#3b4a5c\"/><path d=\"M296.6 181.9 A 100 100 0 0 1 100.0 156.0 L200.0 156.0 A 0 0 0 0 0 200.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#f6e7b8\"/><path d=\"M299.1 142.9 A 100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L249.2 193.7 A 62 62 0 0 0 261.5 147.9 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M113.4 206.0 A 100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L142.7 132.3 A 62 62 0 0 0 146.3 187.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M241.0 197.0 A 58 58 0 0 1 154.0 191.3 L179.4 171.8 A 26 26 0 0 0 218.4 174.4 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M149.8 127.0 A 58 58 0 0 1 253.6 133.8 L224.0 146.1 A 26 26 0 0 0 177.5 143.0 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">00:00</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">06:00</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12:00</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18:00</text><text x=\"275.13776940828177\" y=\"165.74079978861175\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dawn</text><text x=\"118.46016078906504\" y=\"174.78039091448292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusk</text><text x=\"197.80188983779635\" y=\"197.9424404596921\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bedded</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: moving. Peaks near first and last light.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"First light, last light, that's the white tail's right.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 2 hours before dark, 30 minutes before light.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (tradition): \"Be there before the deer, not with the deer.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks, mistakes and field drill</summary><ul><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, widely repeated): \"Hunt the wind you have, not the wind you want.\"</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Moon or no moon, dawn wins soon.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 3 to 1: deer drink about 3 kg of water for each kg of dry food.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Arriving at first light instead of before it.</li><li>Leaving the evening stand early and spooking deer already in the field.</li><li>Skipping a hunt because of the moon chart.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Sit one evening stand from 2 hours before dark to legal end. Note the minute each deer appears. Repeat 3 evenings.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>BC Ministry of Environment, <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/whttail.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">White tailed deer in BC</a> (Blood 2000), via research notes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Stewart and others 2002, <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/jmammal/article/84/3/1076/905056\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">deer activity timing</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Knight, Montana State University Extension, <a href=\"https://animalrangeextension.montana.edu/wildlife/documents/whitetail-mgmt.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">White tailed deer management for Montana landowners</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Auburn University, <a href=\"https://etd.auburn.edu/handle/10415/7077\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">abiotic factors and deer activity, South Carolina</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Mississippi DWFP, <a href=\"https://www.mdwfp.com/media/news/wildlife-hunting/winter-movements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">winter movements</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>SEAFWA journal 2016, <a href=\"https://seafwa.org/journal/2016/movement-moon-white-tailed-deer-activity-and-solunar-events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">movement with the moon</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Outdoor Life, <a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/10-myths-about-deer-movement/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10 myths about deer movement</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Penn State deer studies via the app's <a href=\"#/s/fronts-and-movement\">Weather fronts</a> session (75 to 80%)</li></ul><ul><li>BC <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, page 11 item 38, read directly 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Research log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-white-tailed-deer.md</code>.</li></ul>"]